    "body": "I think I have the same issue (or it's very closely related) on my work code base. The smallest fragment I could come up with is this:\n\n```python\nif False:\n    # fmt: off # some other comment\n    pass\n```\n\nPutting the `fmt: off` comment at the top level does not trigger the issue. It needs to be in a block.\n\nThe code above then results in the following diff output:\n\n```diff\nMode(target_versions={<TargetVersion.PY310: 10>}, line_length=120, string_normalization=False, is_pyi=False, is_ipynb=False, skip_source_first_line=False, magic_trailing_comma=True, python_cell_magics=set(), preview=False, unstable=False, enabled_features=set())\n--- source\n+++ first pass\n@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@\n if False:\n-    # fmt: off # some other comment\n+            # fmt: off # some other comment\n     pass\n--- first pass\n+++ second pass\n@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@\n if False:\n-            # fmt: off # some other comment\n+                # fmt: off # some other comment\n     pass\n```\n\nHTH",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
