    "updated_at": "2025-11-21T22:09:57Z",
    "body": "🔗@alexhernandezgarcia Contextual Linking for Reviewers\nTo help maintainers quickly understand the motivation behind this pull request, I’ve linked it to [https://github.com/psf/black/issues/4841](https://github.com/psf/black/issues/4841), which documents the crash caused by nested fmt: off / fmt: on directives inside comment blocks. This issue has been reproduced with minimal code fragments and traced back to commit b895a73, which introduced changes in how formatting pragmas are handled.\n\nTagging the issue ensures:\n\n🧭 Clear traceability between the bug report and the fix\n🧪 Easier validation against reported test cases\n📜 Historical context for future contributors and maintainers\nIf needed, I’m happy to provide additional test cases or clarify edge scenarios discussed in the issue thread.",
